                           PROJECT OVERVIEW
=========================================================================
I am building DASH OS, which is a GameBoy (DMG) emulator on ESP32-32E hardware
with the following stack: 

Hardware Configuration:
    • MCU: ESP32-D0WD-V3 @ 240MHz, 520KB SRAM (NO PSRAM) 
    • Display: ST7796 480x320 TFT via HSPI @ 80MHz SPI 
    • Storage: MicroSD via VSPI @ 25MHz (after negotiation from 400kHz init) 
    • Input: 8BitDo Micro controller via Bluepad32 BLE stack 
    • Emulator Core: peanut-gb (DMG only, no GBC support yet) 
    • Toolchain: esp32-bluepad32 v4.1.0, GCC 8.4.0 
Critical Constraints:
    • Heap Budget: ~103KB contiguous at boot, ~92KB consumed by buffers, ~11KB remaining 
    • No PSRAM: All data must fit in internal SRAM 
    • Bluepad32 Conflict: Cannot use standard ESP32 BLE libraries (incompatible stacks) 
    • GCC Quirk: Variables must be declared at top of function (C89-style) 
    • TFT_eSPI Quirk: USE_HSPI_PORT causes internal byte-swap; pushColors(swap=true) also swaps (two swaps = cancel out, pass plain RGB565) 

