2. SD Speed Negotiation
Problem: 
SD at 400kHz = 5OKB/s -> 16KB bank read = 330ms -> <2FPS

Solution:
SD.begin(SD_CS, sdspi, 400000);   // SD spec requires 400kHz for init
SD.end();
SD.begin(SD_CS, sdspi, 25000000); // Renegotiate to 25MHz

Performance:
  - 400kHz: 16KB = 330ms -> unusable
  - 25MHz: ~5ms -> 3 bank switches = 15ms overhead per frame
  - ROM fully cached in RAM: 0ms -> 60fps

Why 25MHz? Balance of speed versus stability. 50MHz caused card detection failures. 20MHz/10Hz is
a fallback for fussy cards

