3. 2-Bank LRU Cache with Block Reads

Problem:

Byte-by-Byte SD reads = 450ms per frame (2FPS)

Solution:

IRAM_ATTR uint8_t gb_rom_read(struct gb_s *gb, const uint_fast32_t a) {
  if(a < ROMBANK) return bank0Cache[a];  // Bank 0 always cached
  
  uint32_t base = (a / ROMBANK) * ROMBANK;
  
  // Check bank1 cache
  if(base == bank1Base) {
    bank1LRU = ++lruCounter;
    return bank1Cache[a - base];
  }
  
  // Cache miss - load entire 16KB bank at once
  bank1Base = base;
  bank1LRU = ++lruCounter;
  romf.seek(base);
  romf.read(bank1Cache, min((uint32_t)ROMBANK, romsz - base));
  return bank1Cache[a - base];
}

Performance Improvment:
12.8x speedup (450ms -> 35-67ms per frame)

Why Block Reads Work:
  - Single romf.read(16384) = one SD transaction (~5ms)
  - Byte-by-Byte = 16384 SD transaction (~450ms)
  - Gameboy code has spatial locality which reads seqential bytes

