5. IRAM_ATTR on Hot Path

  IRAM_ATTR uint8_t gb_rom_read(struct gb_s *gb, const uint_fast32_t a)
  IRAM_ATTR void lcd_draw_line(struct gb_s *gb, const uint8_t *px, const uint_fast8_t line)  

Why: These functions are called thousands of times per frame. IRAM_ATTR puts them in fast
Internal RAM instead of flash, eliminating cache misses.

